#    parameter is seeded, the summary no longer claims `result<-0 EXACT`, and the program is
#    REFUSED — "'r' does not live long enough … (E0597)", the escaping borrow named rather than the
#    variance accident. Landed as tests/logos/fail/bc_0917h_ptrland_hb_x1_refuse; the TUPLE-field
#    and ARRAY-field carriers, which were unrowed and ran 8 and 6 on the shipped binary, are closed
#    by the SAME change and landed beside it as hb_x2/hb_x3.
#
# refptr_param_eq_compares_outer_ref — `==` on a `&*mut T` PARAMETER compares the OUTER REFERENCE
#    instead of the pointer, so two copies of one pointer compare unequal: exit 1 where rustc gives 0.
